    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3098" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăpostŏlĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποστολικος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>relating to an apostle</i>, <i>apostolic</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Praescr. adv. Haer. 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">doctrina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpostŏlĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the pupils and friends of the Apostles</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Praescr. adv. Haer 32</span></i>;
				<i>the name of a Christian sect</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Isid. 8, 5, p. 257</span></i> Lind.
		al</div>
